		<profile name="Invocation Of Nehek"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="9219-4a13-f83c-5ae1">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">During the Command sub-phase of their turn, if they are not engaged in combat, this character may attempt to resurrect the fallen by making a Leadership test (using their own Leadership). If this test is passed, a single friendly unit that has the Necromantic Undead special rule and is within 12&quot; of this character recovers a number of lost Wounds. However, magically repairing great Undead beasts is much harder than raising Zombies from the dirt. Therefore, how many Wounds are recovered depends upon the unit’s troop type and this character’s Level of Wizardry:
- If the unit’s troop type is ‘regular infantry’ or ‘heavy infantry’, it recovers a number of Wounds equal to this character’s Level of Wizardry +D3.
- If the unit’s troop type is ‘swarms’, ‘light cavalry’ or ‘war beasts’, it recovers a number of Wounds equal to this character’s Level of Wizardry +1.
- If the unit’s troop type is ‘monstrous infantry’, ‘heavy cavalry’, ‘monstrous cavalry’ or ‘light chariot’, it recovers a number of Wounds equal to this character’s Level of Wizardry.
- If the unit’s troop type is ‘heavy chariot’, ‘monstrous creature’, ‘behemoth’ or ‘war machine’, it recovers a single Wound.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Wight Banner"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="6d9a-a7c4-e899-727a">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">A Gunnery Wight that has been upgraded to be your Battle Standard Bearer replaces the &quot;Hold Your Ground&quot; rule given in the Warhammer: the Old World rulebook with the version given below:
**&quot;Hold Your Ground&quot;:** Friendly units within the Battle Standard Bearer&apos;s Command range may re-roll any failed Leadership test. In addition, friendly units within the Battle Standard Bearer’s Command range reduce the number of Wounds lost due to the Unstable special rule by D3.
*Note that this is not cumulative with the Indomitable (X) special rule. If a unit is affected by both, use the highest value.*</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Bound Spirits"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="90f0-98df-b9e9-934a">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Unlike other swarms, this unit is not subject to the Undisciplined rule. In other words, this unit can use the Inspiring Presence rule of the army’s General and the Hold your Ground rule of a Battle Standard.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Accursed Weapons"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="238e-4e22-63f-9042">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">A hand weapon carried by a model with this special rule has the Magical Attacks special rule and an Armour Piercing characteristic of -1.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Black Powder Weapon"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="238e-4e22-63f-9043">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Zombies are not normally known for their ability to shoot straight (or at all). However, Harkon has long ago woven an enchantment that allows them to do just that. Models with this special rule never apply any modifiers to their rolls To Hit when shooting a black powder weapon, regardless of the source of the modifier. However, any rolls of 1 will result in the gun misfiring - resolve the hit against the firing unit instead of the target. Additionally, all black powder weapons equipped by models with this special rule have the Cumbersome special rule. </characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Gunnery Mob"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="238e-4e22-63f-9f43">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">A stampede of crab-like monsters is a the scarier when accompanied by the hisses and cracks of gunpowder weapons. Rotting Promethean models with this special rule carry two Zombie Gunner Crew riders who may fire in a 360 degree angle like the crew of a chariot. Additionally, models with this special rule count as 'monstrous cavalry' instead of 'monstrous creatures'. </characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Slavering Charge"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="3d49-5f35-1a3-51e9">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">During a turn in which it charged, this model has a +1 modifier to its Strength characteristic.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Balefire Brazier"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="1e33-db54-cb98-d68b">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Enemy Wizards that are within 15&quot; of one or more models with this special rule when attempting to cast a spell must increase that spell’s casting value by 1.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Warped Tintinnabulation"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="fa4e-5cd0-9a0d-adc1">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">When a friendly unit that is within 15&quot; of this model recovers a number of lost Wounds due to a character using the Invocation of Nehek special rule, roll a D6. On a roll of 4+, the unit recovers one additional Wound. In addition, friendly units within 15&quot; of this model reduce the number of Wounds lost due to the Unstable special rule by 1.

*Note that this is cumulative with the Indomitable (X) special rule.*</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Deck Droppers"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="9015-2214-a000-7399">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Although Deck Droppers carry a Zombie,
the Zombie does not fight in close combat so does not have a
separate profile. Instead, it allows the unit to perform a
‘Flying Salvo’ attack against a single enemy unit that is not
engaged in combat. To do so, the Deck Droppers unit must
move (by flying) over the unit it wishes to attack during the
Remaining Moves sub-phase. Once this unit’s movement is
complete, roll a D6 for each Fell Bat in the Deck Droppers
unit. 
1: The Deck Droppers unit suffers Strength 4 hit with an AP of -1 instead
2-3: Complete miss
4-5: Scatter(1d6) 1 3" template starting centered over a model flown over. Risks hit of Strength 4 with an AP of -1
6: Scatter 2 instead</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Bestial Fury"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="9015-2214-a000-7398">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Enemy units cannot claim any bonus combat result points for being engaged with this model’s flank or rear arc.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Dark Vitality"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="4190-a061-b7dc-3712">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Models with this special rule are not subject to the Death of a General rule. In addition, unless they have joined a unit that does not have this special rule they (and their mounts) can march as normal.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
			<modifiers>
				<modifier type="append"
				          value="A Vampire Count or Vampire Captain with this special rule may wear armour without penality."
				          field="9f84-4221-785a-db50">
					<conditions>
						<condition type="atLeast"
						           value="1"
						           field="selections"
						           scope="force"
						           childId="974c-3bf3-af4b-701d"
						           shared="true"
						           includeChildSelections="true"/>
					</conditions>
				</modifier>
			</modifiers>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Indomitable"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="78b6-d212-caa2-cef1">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">A unit with this special rule reduces the number of wounds suffered due to the Unstable special rule by the number shown in brackets (shown here as ‘X’).

Note that this special rule is not cumulative. If two or more models in a unit have this special rule, use the highest value for the entire unit. For example, if a character with Indomitable (2) joins a unit with Indomitable (1), the whole unit uses the character’s Indomitable (2) special rule.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="*Necrofex Colossus Attacks"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="78b6-d212-caa2-cef2">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Instead of attacking normally during the Combat phase, a Necrofex Colossus may choose
to make a ‘Necrofex Attack’. To make a Necrofex Attack, nominate an enemy unit that the
Necrofex Colossus is engaged in combat with to be the target of the attack and roll on the
Necrofex Attacks table below to determine what the Necrofex Colossus does:

1-2: Batter and Slash: The Necrofex flails and smashes at its enemies with its massive
limbs. The Necrofex Colossus fights using the Random Attacks (D6+1) special
rule.

3-4: Impale: The Necrofex Colossus impales the foe with its misshapen claw and tries
to strip their soul from their body. Select one model in base contact; that model,
and all models in the same file, must pass an Initiative test or suffer a Strength 7
Hit with the Monster Slayer special rule.

5-6: Screams of the Damned: Roll 2D6 and add the number of Wounds the Necrofex
Colossus has left. For each point by which the result exceeds the target unit's
Leadership, the target unit suffers 1 Wound with no armour saves allowed.
Wounds suffered from it are distributed as from shooting.

</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Vortex of Death"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="78b6-d212-caa2-cef3">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Whilst within 12" of a Necrofex Colossus, any model (friend or foe) attempting to cast a spell
from the Lore of Necromancy, Lore of Death, or Lore of the Deep may apply a +1 modifier to any Casting roll they make. In
addition, a Wizard mounted on a Necrofex Colossus increases their Dispel range by 3"</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Gun Arm"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="78b6-d212-caa2-cef4">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">The Necrofex Colossus is equipped with a Carronade (see the Carronade unit entry). If a
‘Misfire’ is rolled on the Artillery dice, this model loses a single Wound (instead of rolling on a
Misfire table). </characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Screams of the damned"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="78b6-d212-caa2-cef5">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">A Necrofex Colossus with this upgrade gains the Wailing Dirge special rule</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Watery Grave"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="78b6-d212-caa2-cef6">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">All open ground within 8" of a Necrofex Colossus with this upgrade counts as a water feature
and difficult terrain. </characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Necromantic Undead"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="a6ee-a62b-1579-2c37">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Models with this special rule are ‘Undead’. Undead models cannot march (unless they have the Fly (X) special rule and choose to move by flying). In addition, all Undead models have the following universal special rules:
- Fear
- Immune to Psychology
- Unbreakable
- Unstable A character with this special rule cannot join a unit without this special rule, and vice versa.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Tumescent Surprise"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="a6ee-a62b-1579-2c38">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">As the enemy draws near, mobs of Pirate Zombies release Bloated Corpses to wreak explosive havoc on the enemy. Bloated Corpses are not placed on the battlefield at the start of the game. Instead, make a note of which Zombie Pirate units include Bloated Corpses, and of how many they include. These units are referred to as ‘concealing’ units. A concealing unit may release one or more of its Bloated Corpses during any Start of Turn sub-phase. When a Bloated Corpses is released, it runs outwards of the horde to appear at one of the units edges. To represent this, place the model so that it is in full base contact with at least one model from its concealing unit and not touching the bases of any enemy models. A Bloated Corpse can move and declare charges normally after it has been released, acting as an independent unit.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Gaseous Demise"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="a6ee-a62b-1bb9-2c38">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Fu of the miasma of decomposition, Bloated Corpses are just a wound away from erupting in a rancid last of rotten flesh. If at any point a Bloated Corpse loses its wound or makes base contact with any enemy model, it immediately throws itself to the ground, bursting in a disgusting explosion of putrid remains and noxious gases. Centre a 3" blast template over the Bloated Corpse model. Every model (friend or foe) whose base lies underneath the template risks being hit (as described on page 95 of the Core Rule Book) and suffering a single Strength 6 hit with no Armour Save allowed (Ward and Regeneration saves can be attempted as normal).</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Fire!!!"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="a6ee-a62b-1579-2c39">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Any units of Zombies or Deck Gunners within the Command
range of one or more Wights can reactive fire with non ponderous or move and shoot weapons.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="The Newly Dead"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="4176-fb21-2d35-b9c9">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">When resurrecting the fallen, a unit with this special rule can be taken beyond its starting size (but not beyond its maximum size).</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Aquatic"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="1f39-2789-f136-7645">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Models with this special rule do not suffer any modifiers to their Movement characteristic when moving through any difficult or dangerous terrain feature which has been designated a ‘water feature’. This might include shallow streams or fords, swampy ground, fast flowing rivers, ponds or lakes, and players should agree prior to the game if any terrain is a water feature.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Wailing Dirge"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="522d-e0c9-a174-ca95">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">During the Shooting phase of its turn, unless it marched during the preceding Movement phase, a model with this special rule may make a ‘Wailing Dirge’ attack. A Wailing Dirge attack may target any enemy unit that is within 8&quot; of this model (including units that are engaged in combat) and that this model can draw a line of sight to, or that this model is engaged in combat with.

The target must make a Leadership test with a -2 modifier to its Leadership characteristic (to a minimum of 2). If this test is failed, the target suffers a number of wounds equal to the amount by which it failed the test, with no armour or Regeneration saves permitted (Ward saves can be attempted as normal).

Note that a Wailing Dirge attack can target an enemy character, regardless of the usual rules for targeting Lone characters.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
			<modifiers>
				<modifier type="set"
				          value="During the Shooting phase of its turn, unless it marched during the preceding Movement phase, a model with this special rule may make a ‘Wailing Dirge’ attack. A Wailing Dirge attack may target any enemy unit that is within 8&quot; of this model (including units that are engaged in combat) and that this model can draw a line of sight to. If this model is engaged in combat, it may only target a unit in base contact.


The target must make a Leadership test with a -2 modifier to its Leadership characteristic (to a minimum of 2). If this test is failed, the target suffers a number of wounds equal to the amount by which it failed the test, with no armour or Regeneration saves permitted (Ward saves can be attempted as normal).


Note that a Wailing Dirge attack can target an enemy character, regardless of the usual rules for targeting Lone characters."
				          field="9f84-4221-785a-db50">
					<comment>Renegades</comment>
					<conditions>
						<condition type="atLeast"
						           value="1"
						           field="selections"
						           scope="force"
						           childId="974c-3bf3-af4b-701d"
						           shared="true"
						           includeChildSelections="true">
							<comment>Renegades</comment>
						</condition>
					</conditions>
				</modifier>
			</modifiers>
		</profile>
		<profile name="Resurrecting The Fallen"
		         typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673"
		         typeName="Special Rule"
		         hidden="false"
		         id="c1d3-29e3-b7cd-c9f7"
		         page="154"
		         publicationId="7c89-736c-3139-24a0">
			<characteristics>
				<characteristic name="Description"
				                typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">•	First, any characters that have joined the unit are healed. A character that has been reduced to zero Wounds and removed from play cannot be resurrected.

•	Second, models with more than one Wound on their profile are healed.

•	Next, the unit champion is resurrected, displacing rank-and-file models as required, followed by the standard bearer and musician.

•	Finally, rank-and-file models are resurrected.

Note that, in the case of multiple Wound models, each model must be fully healed, recovering all of its lost Wounds, before another can be healed or resurrected.

Note also that at least one model must remain in order for a unit to be healed. In other words, a unit that has been reduced to zero Wounds and removed from play cannot be resurrected.

Resurrected models are added to the front rank until it reaches the minimum required to claim a Rank Bonus, after which additional models can be added to the front or rear rank. If the unit already has more than one rank, models can only be added to the rear rank. A unit cannot be taken beyond its starting size.</characteristic>
			</characteristics>
		</profile>
